.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Reads triangulated render meshes of surfaces output from Rhinoceros (McNeel&Associates) and converts them into a 3D \fBVSet\fP that can be read by CSMP\&.

.PP
Multiple surfaces are distinguished using the object names from Rhino\&.

.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
S\&. K\&. Matthai 
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
2002 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void csmp::RhinoSurfaceReader::ExchangeCoordinateAxes (int axis_a, int axis_b)"
Swaps the specified coordinate axis which are assumed to be labeled 0=x, 1=y, and 2=z\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The two integer arguments refer to the axis which shall be changed\&. 
.br
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To adapt surface data to another frame of reference\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
If the axes do not exist (are below 0 or greater than 2) the method will quit emitting a message\&. 
.SS "void csmp::RhinoSurfaceReader::MoveCoordinates (double x_move, double y_move, double z_move)"
Moves the triangle coordinates by the specified amounts in the x, y, and z, directions\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The three method arguments specify the amount by which each point coordinate is to be moved\&. A value of zero leaves the coordinates in place\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To transform the stored surfaces to another space position\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
If no objects are stored, Nothing is done\&. 
.SS "void csmp::RhinoSurfaceReader::ScaleCoordinates (double x_fac, double y_fac, double z_fac)"
Muliplies the triangle coordinates by the supplied factors and reorganises the triangles if their sense of rotation changes\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The scale factors for the x, y, and z axis are entered\&. A factor of
.IP "1." 4
is to be entered if an axis shall not be scaled and a factor of -1\&. if an axis shall be inverted\&.
.PP
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To scale an object for a new frame of reference\&. 
.br
.SH "Messages"
.PP
Nothing is done if no objects are present\&. 
.SS "void csmp::RhinoSurfaceReader::WriteObjectsToTSurf (const char * tsurf_file, const char * GEOLOGICAL_TYPE = \fR'fault'\fP) const"

.PP
GoCAD output: TSurf format: all surfaces in the file\&. Writes all objects from the Rhino output file into a single Gocad file\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Not necessarily recommended since GoCad often has difficulties in reading individual surfaces\&. 
.SS "void csmp::RhinoSurfaceReader::WriteObjectToTSurf (const char * obj, std::ofstream & ) const"

.PP
GoCAD output: TSurf format: a single selected surface\&. The surface will be written to file without associating any properties with it\&. 
.SS "void csmp::RhinoSurfaceReader::WriteSelectedObjectsToTSurf (const char * tsurf_file) const"

.PP
GoCAD output: TSurf format: surfaces selected by the user through stdin\&. Writes a series of files which contain one surface each corresponding to the selected surfaces from the Rhino '\&.raw' dataset\&. The names of the objects are appended to the output file names which start with the supplied file name\&. A hyphen is put between the filename and the object name\&. 

